  "goodToKnow": "Der Lebensraum means habitat in biology: Lebensräume schützen, der Lebensraum des Luchses. It can also mean living space for people. Be aware of its history: the Nazis used Lebensraum im Osten as the slogan for conquering and colonising Eastern Europe, and English borrowed the word with that meaning. In modern German, its neutral ecological use is normal, but in political contexts it can still sound loaded. Plural: die Lebensräume."
